# A parameter step is setParam's retrying request, and the vehicle's echo is what ends it.
#
# The editor's + and - write RTL_ALT through the link's request, which puts PARAM_SET on the wire
# and sends it again every 700 ms, up to three times, until the vehicle echoes the parameter -
# setParamAsync's loop. The link counts every send, and params.write.sends publishes the count
# for the last write to end. `ExtLibs/ArduPilot/Mavlink/MAVLinkInterface.cs:1638-1770`
#
# SITL does not drop packets, so against it the count is one: this proves the path - the step is
# a request the link counts, SITL's echo ends it, and the status line says what the vehicle now
# holds - not the retry. The retry itself, a lost first send answered by a second, is proven
# against a scripted vehicle that loses it: crates/mp-gui/src/params.rs,
# a_write_whose_first_send_is_lost_is_sent_again_and_confirmed.
#
# Needs SITL (a copter): tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/params-retry.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760
screen params
window 1600x1200
budget 50
# A config.xml of its own, so the "Show me again?" boxes this script clicks are not already
# suppressed by the settings of the machine running it.
env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
# RawParamWarning, on the Full Parameter List's Activate (ConfigRawParams.cs:92): "Show me
# again?" unticked, so no later visit asks, and OK.
# The vehicle first: a click before its first heartbeat is a click the screen may forget
# (vehicle.connected only says the link is open).
expect vehicle.count > 0
click raw-param-warning-again
click raw-param-warning-ok
click param-download
expect params.held > 500
# Nothing written yet.
expect params.write.outcome none
# This SITL (Copter 4.7-dev) names the parameter RTL_ALT_M; older firmware says RTL_ALT.
# The tree lists every group; RTL lies below a 1200-pixel window: wheeled into view.
reveal params-tree param-group-RTL
click param-group-RTL
click param-RTL_ALT_M
click param-step-+
expect params.write.name RTL_ALT_M
expect params.write.outcome accepted
expect params.write.sends 1
expect status ~ RTL_ALT_M =
# And back to where it was, the same way.
click param-step--
expect params.write.name RTL_ALT_M
expect params.write.outcome accepted
expect params.write.sends 1
